Subject: module-allow-symbol-crc-mismatch

The factory vendor modules were built against Google's stock kernel. Permit a
module CRC mismatch while retaining a visible warning. The kernel release and
task layout are still held to the factory values.

Source: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common commit bd23337e42e794964a89f47596daf1209a25ee1a

--- a/kernel/module/version.c
+++ b/kernel/module/version.c
@@ -68,8 +68,8 @@
 	return 1;
 
 bad_version:
-	pr_warn("%s: disagrees about version of symbol %s\n", info->name, symname);
-	return 0;
+	pr_warn("%s: disagrees about version of symbol %s (allowed)\n", info->name, symname);
+	return 1;
 }
 
 int check_modstruct_version(const struct load_info *info,

